      "inputTokens": 126,
      "outputTokens": 1069,
      "costUsd": 0.009684,
      "pronunciationText": "Now put an inside in. Find the integral of fifteen cos five x. Try sine five x. On the graph, that's sine x squashed sideways by a factor of five, so every slope is multiplied by five. Its derivative is five cos five x. We need fifteen cos five x, which is three times as much. So the answer is three sine five x, plus C. Differentiate back: three times five cos five x is fifteen cos five x. It's the same cause as the last two videos. A linear inside multiplies the gradient by its rate, so the primitive divides by it."
