      "inputTokens": 112,
      "outputTokens": 841,
      "costUsd": 0.007625,
      "pronunciationText": "Back to the solar panels. With t in hours after sunrise, their power is five sine of pi t over twelve kilowatts. The inner rate is pi over twelve, so divide by it. The energy is minus sixty over pi, times cos of pi t over twelve, plus C. At sunrise the energy is zero, and cos of zero is one, so C is sixty over pi. By noon, that's about nineteen kilowatt hours. By sunset, double that, about thirty-eight. Half the day's energy comes before noon."
    },
