      "outputTokens": 884,
      "costUsd": 0.008019,
      "pronunciationText": "Next, the integral of two sec squared, of two x minus pi over three. The inside has rate two, and the two in front matches it. So the answer is just tan of two x minus pi over three, plus C. Check: its derivative is two sec squared of two x minus pi over three. The minus pi over three is a slide, and a slide changes no slopes. Keep the asymptotes. They're where two x minus pi over three equals pi over two, plus any multiple of pi. That's at x equals five pi over twelve, and every pi over two from there."
